11. Machine Learning & Predictive Analytics

Machine learning techniques were used to perform predictive analytics on the e-commerce sales data.

Two machine learning models were implemented.

Models Used
Linear Regression

Linear Regression was implemented as a baseline predictive model for estimating sales.

Random Forest Regressor

Random Forest Regressor was implemented to capture more complex relationships between the available features and sales.

12. Model Training

The dataset was divided into training and testing data.

The training dataset was used to train the machine learning models.

The testing dataset was used to evaluate model performance on unseen data.

The models were trained using relevant numerical and engineered features available in the dataset.

13. Model Evaluation

The machine learning models were evaluated using standard regression evaluation metrics.

Mean Absolute Error (MAE)

MAE measures the average absolute difference between actual and predicted values.

MAE = Mean(|Actual - Predicted|)

Lower MAE indicates better prediction accuracy.

Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)

RMSE measures the square root of the average squared prediction error.

RMSE = √Mean((Actual - Predicted)²)

Lower RMSE indicates better model performance.

R² Score

R² Score indicates how well the model explains the variation in the target variable.

A higher R² Score indicates better explanatory performance.

