Real-time sales monitoring.
Distributed big-data technologies for larger datasets.

26. Conclusion

The E-Commerce Sales Analytics & Predictive Intelligence project demonstrates an end-to-end data analytics and predictive intelligence workflow.

A dataset containing 100,000 e-commerce transaction records was analyzed using Python, SQL, SQLite, machine learning, and Power BI.

The project includes data preprocessing, feature engineering, exploratory data analysis, SQL business analysis, machine learning model development, model evaluation, sales prediction, feature importance analysis, and interactive dashboard development.

Two predictive models, Linear Regression and Random Forest Regressor, were implemented and compared using MAE, RMSE, and R² Score.

The Power BI dashboard brings together important business KPIs, sales trends, customer analysis, product performance, predictive results, model comparison, and feature importance into an interactive visualization platform.

Overall, the project demonstrates how data analytics and predictive intelligence techniques can transform raw e-commerce transaction data into meaningful business insights and support data-driven decision-making.

